sam.docs: quick check-in 1 updating a few SDK snippets in the docs repo for streaming + pagination across py/ts/go. tiny behavioral clarifications but no API break. PR: https://github.com/redwood/inference-docs/pull/5012
lia-sdk: can you list the concrete snippet changes so i can run them through the example test-suite?
sam.docs: sure 1 python now uses the context-managed stream helper (`with client.stream_chat(...) as s:`) so sockets are closed deterministically. TS switches to an AsyncIterator return instead of passing callbacks. Go ensures resume tokens are cloned per request to avoid shared buffer reuse. snippets below: 
```py
with client.stream_chat("Tell me a joke") as stream:
  for event in stream:
    if event.type == 'delta':
      print(event.delta)
```
```ts
for await (const ev of client.streamResponses(request)) {
  if (ev.type === 'delta') console.log(ev.delta)
}
```
```go
// clone resume token to avoid reusing underlying bytes
token := resume.Clone()
for {
  page, err := client.List(ctx, token)
  if err != nil { return err }
  token = page.NextToken.Clone()
}
```
omar-eng: nice. CI found one stale example using the old generator pattern (AttributeError: 'generator' object has no __enter__). it's in docs/quickstarts/streaming.md line ~91.
sam.docs: thanks, fixed that reference and removed an unused import causing flake8. also added a one-liner in migration.md: "When migrating, prefer connection-level retries; rely on resume tokens for application-level continuation to prevent double-submitting user inputs."
harper: small wording nit: prefer "resume token" everywhere (not "continuation token").
lia-sdk: added a short note about idempotency: "If requests are not idempotent, avoid automatic retrying of the payload; use resume tokens for partial resumes."
